            "question": "Can I convert HEIC back to original quality?",
            "answer": "No, converting HEIC to JPG and back won't restore original quality. Each conversion between lossy formats causes cumulative quality loss. Always keep original HEIC files as backup if staying in Apple ecosystem. If you need to share photos, convert HEIC to JPG once at high quality (90-95) and keep both versions. Don't convert back and forth."
