            "description": "Logos, icons, and interface elements with transparency.",
            "content": "PNG is the gold standard for web graphics. Use PNG-32 for logos and UI elements with alpha transparency (aim for <200KB). Use PNG-8 for simple icons with limited colors (2-256 colors) - can achieve 50-70% smaller files. Avoid PNG for photos without transparency - use JPEG or WebP instead for 50-80% smaller files.",
